# Renders stay out; build inputs stay in. Mirrors the repository root
# .gitignore (rule changed 2026-09-18): anything the pipeline PRODUCED from a
# beat sheet goes to Google Drive; anything used to BUILD the video -- screen
# captures, source recordings, sfx, pantry stills and clips, fixtures -- is
# committed here. So nothing below is excluded by file type, only by location
# or by render suffix. The root file already covers the render folders; they
# are repeated so this folder stays safe if it is copied out on its own.

# renders
mp3/
audio/
media/
clips/
manim/
exports/
renders/
_qc/
*-slate.mp4
*-cut.mp4
*-review.mp4
*-topaz.mp4
*-8k.mp4

# the named 16:9 / 9:16 masters are renders too; they live in Drive
*_16x9.mp4
*_9x16.mp4

# local build state
build-state.json
*.verified.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# week-05: handoff masters follow docs/FELLOWS-SUBMISSION.md -- ProjectName_VolunteerName.mp4,
# one folder per aspect (handoff/landscape, handoff/vertical) so the two cuts cannot overwrite
# each other. Renders; they live in Drive. NOTE: vertical/ itself is the full-length 9:16
# companion's SOURCE folder (./art vertical) -- its beat sheet is committed; its mp3/media/clips
# are caught by the render rules above.
handoff/
*.mp4.verified.json

# an excerpt of the HyperFrames render (kept as evidence of the captions) is itself a
# render: rendered video goes to Drive, even when small (FELLOWS-SUBMISSION.md)
pantry/hf-captions-clip.mp4
